{title: Turn Your Eyes upon Jesus}
{lyricist: Helen H. Lemmel}
{composer: Helen H. Lemmel}
{year: 1922}
{key: D}
{meta: tune LEMMEL}
{meta: variation The hymn, sung to LEMMEL}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: tags devotion, invitation}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
O [D]soul, are you weary and [Em]troubled?
[A7]No light in the darkness you [D]see?
There's [D]light for a look at the [G]Savior,
And [D]life more a[A7]bundant and [D]free!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[D]Turn your eyes upon [Em]Jesus,
[A7]Look full in His wonderful [D]face,
And the [D]things of earth will grow [G]strangely dim,
In the [D]light of His [A7]glory and [D]grace.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Through [D]death into life ever[Em]lasting
[A7]He passed, and we follow Him [D]there;
O'er [D]us sin no more hath do[G]minion,
For [D]more than con[A7]querors we [D]are!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
His [D]word shall not fail you, He [Em]promised;
[A7]Believe Him, and all will be [D]well;
Then [D]go to a world that is [G]dying,
His [D]perfect sal[A7]vation to [D]tell!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
